  "design": [
    "Six synthetic questions with objectively verifiable answers; q1-q4 are exploration, q5-q6 are untouched validation (not measured until the exploration patterns are recorded).",
    "Each question is run under two answer-letter mappings: m1 A=correct(K) B=competing(T) C=X D=Y; m2 A=T B=K C=Y D=X. The same semantic answer changes letter.",
    "Variations: NEUTRAL (unrelated prose), RELEVANT (on-topic text that mentions the competing subject, no evidence), COMPETING (explicit competing evidence for T), NEGATED (evidence against T), REPEATED (the competing claim stated twice).",
    "Fragments never mention answer letters; the same candidate file is used under both mappings. Lengths are matched by neutral on-topic padding; residual token mismatches are recorded in token_match."
  ]
}
